menu "Heart Beacon"

    choice HB_HW
        prompt "Carrier board"
        default HB_HW_A
        help
            Rev A: the hand-built carrier the deployed beacons use (pixels on GPIO2, battery on GPIO3, LEDs
            always powered). Rev B: the 2026-11 board (ESP32_heart.brd) with the LED load switch, the LIS3DH
            and USB sense. Build it with SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.revb".
            Rev C: the single-sided 48 x 37 mm board for the 91 mm brass heart (ESP32_heart_revC3), with the GPIO map
            its routing needed: pixels GPIO21, LED switch GPIO20, SCL GPIO2. sdkconfig.revc.

        config HB_HW_A
            bool "Rev A"
        config HB_HW_B
            bool "Rev B"
        config HB_HW_C
            bool "Rev C"
    endchoice

    config HB_BTN_GPIO
        int "Button GPIO (active low, internal pull-up)"
        range 0 5
        default 0
        help
            Must be one of GPIO0-5: only those can wake the ESP32-C3 from deep sleep.

    config HB_LED_PWR_GPIO
        int "LED rail load-switch GPIO (high = on), -1 = none"
        range -1 21
        default 7 if HB_HW_B
        default 20 if HB_HW_C
        default -1
        help
            Rev B: GPIO7 drives Q5, which turns on the P-FET Q6 in the LED rail; R8 keeps it off in reset and
            deep sleep. -1 on rev A (LEDs always powered). On rev A a free pin (GPIO10) can stand in for a
            bench check of the switching: the transitions log at debug level.

    config HB_HAS_XTAL32K
        bool "32 kHz crystal fitted"
        depends on HB_HW_A
        default n
        help
            The SuperMini has none. A crystal occupies GPIO0/1 and needs RTC_CLK_SRC_EXT_CRYS; rev B uses
            GPIO1 for the LIS3DH interrupt.

    config HB_BATT_DIV_X1000
        int "Battery divider ratio x 1000 (calibrate per unit)"
        range 1000 4000
        default 2000
        help
            Battery voltage = ADC pin voltage x this / 1000. Both revs use two equal resistors (rev B 1 MOhm
            each, which reads a little low through the ADC's input leakage): trim against a meter.

    config HB_LED_WS2811_400K
        bool "LED timing: true 400 kHz (WS2811)"
        default n
        help
            n: the waveform v1 actually sends. v1 asks Adafruit NeoPixel for NEO_KHZ400, but on
            arduino-esp32 3.x (IDF 5) the library's esp.c ignores the speed flag and always sends
            0.4/0.8 us symbols (1.2 us per bit). y: the 400 kHz WS2811 timing (0.5/2.0 and 1.2/1.3 us)
            the library used on IDF 4. Switch only if the bench shows wrong colours.

    config HB_BENCH_FAST_NAP
        bool "Bench: nap after 1 min idle, wake every 1 min"
        default n
        help
            Overrides pwr.idle_nap_min and pwr.nap_wake_min so the bench can see NAP, the timer wake and
            the button wake in minutes. Never ship with this on.

endmenu
